course: dictionary
lesson: 10201
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Tint can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is a slight shade of a colour, a pale or light version of it. As a verb, it means to add a light colour to something.
explain: «Adding white to a colour makes a lighter tint; adding black makes a darker shade.» Here tint is a noun. The clue is the word white: a tint is what you get when you add white to a colour. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence best.
explain: Tint can also mean a dye for hair, or the dark film on car windows and sunglasses that keeps out the sun. «Algae grow in grooves in sloth fur, giving it a greenish tint that may help it hide from harpy eagles.» Here a tint is a slight colour. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Tint (noun) means a slight shade of a colour, a pale or light version of it.
fact: Tint (verb) means to add a light colour to something.
fact: In art, a tint is made by adding white to a colour, and a shade is made by adding black.
fact: Tinted windows and tinted sunglasses have a dark film that keeps out the sun.
fact: The words around tint, such as white, hair or windows, are the clues that tell you which meaning is meant.
exercise: «The sky had a pink tint at sunset.» What does tint mean here? | A dark film that keeps out the sun | To paint the whole sky with a big brush | A pink rope used to tie up a boat | *A slight shade of pink
exercise: Mia says, «I want to tint my hair blue for the show.» What does tint mean here? | To cut hair short | To curl hair into ringlets | *To colour hair with a dye | To wash hair in cold water
exercise: «Adding white to a colour makes a lighter tint.» How do you make a tint in art? | Mix it with water | *Add white | Add brown | Add black
test: «The car had tinted windows, so nobody could see inside.» Why were the windows tinted? | To clean the glass | To make them shiny | To make them bigger | *To keep out the sun and hide the inside
test: What is the difference between a tint and a shade? | *A tint is made by adding white, and a shade is made by adding black | They mean exactly the same thing | A tint is darker and a shade is lighter | A tint is a type of glass
exam: Which sentence uses tint as a verb? | «The sloth had a greenish tint in its fur.» | «Her hair tint was bright red.» | «The car windows had a dark tint.» | *«She wanted to tint the wall a pale yellow.»
